<item><title>Senegalese journalist Bada Mbathie wins continental local-governance prize</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/senegalese-journalist-bada-mbathie-wins-continental-local-dbfbe2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/senegalese-journalist-bada-mbathie-wins-continental-local-dbfbe2/</guid><category>Senegal</category><description>The Le Soleil reporter was honoured for a story on young residents cleaning Thiaroye Kaw, where their association says members fund its equipment.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:41:57 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" length="32606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Senegal’s under-17s draw 1-1 with Croatia after red card</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/senegal-s-under-17s-draw-1-1-with-croatia-after-red-card-7bb7ef/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/senegal-s-under-17s-draw-1-1-with-croatia-after-red-card-7bb7ef/</guid><category>Senegal</category><description>Sega Fall Mbodji equalised before half-time in Doha, rescuing a point after Senegal conceded in the eighth minute and lost a player.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:37:06 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" length="32606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Senegal&apos;s sanitation office funds toilets for 505 households in Rufisque and Keur Massar</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/senegal-s-sanitation-office-funds-toilets-for-505-441c6d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/senegal-s-sanitation-office-funds-toilets-for-505-441c6d/</guid><category>Senegal</category><description>The works are part of the Dakar Autonomous Sanitation Project, which the state subsidises by more than 90% with French development aid.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:39:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" length="32606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Faye puts Senegal’s revised 2026 budget into force by decree</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/faye-puts-senegal-s-revised-2026-budget-into-force-by-decree-5787b2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/faye-puts-senegal-s-revised-2026-budget-into-force-by-decree-5787b2/</guid><category>Senegal</category><description>The president bypassed repeated parliamentary rejections as the government negotiates a proposed $2.2 billion IMF programme over 36 months.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:43:27 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/faye-puts-senegal-s-revised-2026-budget-into-force-by-decree-5787b2/share.jpg" length="40944" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sn/faye-puts-senegal-s-revised-2026-budget-into-force-by-decree-5787b2/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
